{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 28, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "**A Whirlwind in Japan: Cherry Blossoms and Neon Lights**\n\nJapan stole my heart in a week. It began in **Kyoto**, where ancient temples whispered stories of samurai and geisha. Walking through **Fushimi Inari Shrine**, thousands of red torii gates stretched like a never-ending tunnel, each step deeper into history. The cherry blossoms—*sakura*—painted the streets pastel pink, a fleeting reminder of nature’s beauty.\n\nFrom Kyoto, I raced to **Tokyo**, where tradition and futurism collide. Neon lights pulsed in **Shibuya Crossing**, the world’s busiest intersection, while quiet tea houses in **Asakusa** offered a moment of calm. I lost myself in **Akihabara’s** electric maze of anime shops and arcade games, then escaped to **teamLab Planets**, where digital art turned the floor into a wading pool of light.\n\nA bullet train zipped me to **Osaka**, where towering **Dotonbori** signs glowed like a carnival at night. Street food—takoyaki, okonomiyaki—was crispy, savory perfection. The next morning, I stood at **Osaka Castle**, its stone walls guarding centuries of samurai legacy.\n\nJapan’s magic lies in its contrasts: serene gardens next to skyscrapers, sushi bars beside shrines. Every bite, every temple, every train ride felt like a gift. I left with a suitcase full of souvenirs—and a heart full of memories. **Arigatou, Japan.** I’ll be back.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.06550939381122589}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.27843376994132996}, {"token": " Wh", "logprob": -0.037113383412361145}, {"token": "irl", "logprob": -0.018043426796793938}, {"token": "wind", "logprob": -4.7801782784517854e-05}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -1.6305687427520752}, {"token": " Japan", "logprob": -0.4624401330947876}, {"token": ":", "logprob": -0.10686726123094559}, {"token": " Cherry", "logprob": -0.724677324295044}, {"token": " Bl", "logprob": -